|{{ja-r|勲%等|くん%とう}}: [[order]] of [[merit]]
|{{ja-r|降%等|こう%とう}}: a [[reduction]] in [[rank]]; to [[reduce]] a [[rank]]
|{{ja-r|高%等|こう%とう}}: [[high]] [[rank]], [[high-grade]]
|{{ja-r|劣%等|れっ%とう}}: inferior
}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|など|alt=抔:obsolete}}
From earlier {{m|ja|なんど|tr=nando||etc., and so forth, and such like}}, from earlier {{m|ja|何と|tr=nani to|lit=and what||etc., and so forth, and such like}}, itself a compound of {{m|ja|何|tr=nani||what}} + {{m|ja|と|tr=to||and}}.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref><ref name="DJR">{{R:Daijirin}}</ref><ref name="DJS">{{R:Daijisen}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|など}}

====Adverb====
{{ja-pos|adverb|など}}

# [[et cetera]], that [[kind]] of thing, [[and so on]]
#: {{ja-uxi|[[魚]][[や]][[肉]]'''等'''|さかな や にく '''など'''|fish and meat '''and things like that'''}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{ja-uk|kana=hira|など}}
* For the ''et cetera'' sense, the reading ''tō'' is somewhat more formal than ''nado''. Spelling this term in hiragana is advantageous as it clearly distinguishes it from the formal Sino‐Japanese reading, preventing unintended shifts in tone and providing a visual cue for parsing lists.

===Etymology 3===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|なんど}}
From earlier {{m|ja|何と|tr=nani to|lit=and what||etc., and so forth, and such like}}, itself a compound of {{m|ja|何|tr=nani||what}} + {{m|ja|と|tr=to||and}}.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref><ref name="DJR">{{R:Daijirin}}</ref><ref name="DJS">{{R:Daijisen}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|なんど}}

====Adverb====
{{ja-pos|adverb|なんど}}

# {{lb|ja|sort=なんど|archaic|mostly|_|obsolete}} [[et cetera]], that [[kind]] of thing, and so on

=====Usage notes=====
Largely [[supersede]]d by the ''nado'' reading above.

May be spelled in hiragana, as {{m|ja|なんど}}.

===Etymology 4===
{{ja-kanjitab|yomi=k|ら}}
From {{inh|ja|ojp|-|sort=ら}}. Likely related to {{ja-r|-ろ}}.

====Pronunciation====
{{ja-pron|ら}}

====Suffix====
{{ja-pos|suffix|ら}}

# {{ng|[[pluralizer]]}}
#: {{syn|ja|{{ja-r|達|-たち}}|{{ja-r|共|-ども}}}}
#: {{ja-uxi|[[我]] → 我'''ら'''|われ → われ'''ら'''|I → '''we'''}}
#: {{ja-uxi|[[これ]] → これ'''ら'''|this → '''these'''}}
# {{ng|[[qualifier]], [[softener]]}}: [[around]], [[about]]
#: {{ja-uxi|[[今日]]'''等'''|きょう'''ら'''|roughly today}}
#: {{ja-uxi|[[そこ]]'''等'''[[辺]]|そこ'''ら''' へん|that area '''around''' there}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{ja-uk|kana=hira|ら}}
* Spelling this suffix in hiragana visually distinguishes it from the kanji's formal Sino‐Japanese reading, {{ja-r|等|とう}}, which can also occupy the same grammatical position.
* Attached to words referring to people, the pluralizer may be slightly humbling or derogatory (though not to the extent of {{ja-r|共|-ども}}).

